債資產比率 = 54.5%"},{"id":6,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"流動比率 = 2.78"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":43.91,"default_fair_val":43.91,"premium_pct":155.7,"is_undervalued":false,"pe_trailing":24,"pe_forward":21.1,"pb_trailing":38.4,"pb_forward":34.6,"div_yield":0.02,"ps_ratio":6.6,"fcf_to_ev":3.96,"fcf_to_mcap":3.8,"liab_to_assets":54.5,"cash_to_assets":72.4,"current_ratio":2.78,"roe":-96.2,"roa":-43.7,"moat":{"ticker":"RYTM","period":"2026Q3","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals 的品牌定價權極為薄弱。其核心產品 Setmelanotide 雖然在罕見病領域具有獨特性，但其高昂的價格和有限的適應症限制了其廣泛的市場接受度。公司面臨的挑戰在於，其產品的價值主張難以支撐持續的價格溢價，尤其是在缺乏強大品牌忠誠度的情況下。與其他藥品相比，其品牌影響力不足以構成顯著的定價壁壘，未來若有競爭者進入，其定價能力將面臨更大壓力。","comment_en":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals' brand pricing power is extremely weak. While its core product, Setmelanotide, has uniqueness in the rare disease space, its high price and limited indications restrict broad market acceptance. The company's challenge lies in its value proposition struggling to support sustained price premiums, especially without strong brand loyalty. Compared to other pharmaceuticals, its brand influence is insufficient to form a significant pricing barrier. Future competitors entering the market will exert greater pressure on its pricing capabilities."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals 在專利與監管壁壘方面具有一定的優勢。其核心藥物 Setmelanotide 擁有專利保護，這在短期內提供了市場獨佔性，使其能夠從研發投入中獲取回報。然而，生物製藥領域的專利懸崖風險始終存在，且監管審批的複雜性也可能帶來不確定性。儘管如此，在專利有效期內，這構成了相對穩固的護城河，使其能夠在特定市場中維持競爭優勢。","comment_en":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals possesses a certain advantage in patent and regulatory barriers. Its core drug, Setmelanotide, benefits from patent protection, providing market exclusivity in the short term and allowing it to recoup R&D investments. However, the risk of patent cliffs in the biopharmaceutical sector always exists, and the complexity of regulatory approvals can also introduce uncertainty. Nevertheless, during the patent's validity period, this constitutes a relatively solid moat, enabling it to maintain a competitive edge in specific markets."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals 的轉換成本壁壘非常低。對於患者而言，一旦開始使用 Setmelanotide 並獲得療效，更換藥物的意願可能不高，但這更多是基於療效而非轉換成本。醫療機構和保險公司在選擇藥物時，會考量成本效益與可替代性。由於缺乏顯著的技術綁定或整合需求，患者、醫生或支付方轉換到其他治療方案的阻力不大，這使得公司難以依賴轉換成本來鎖定客戶。","comment_en":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals' switching cost barrier is very low. For patients, once they start using Setmelanotide and achieve therapeutic effects, the willingness to switch medications might not be high, but this is more due to efficacy rather than switching costs. Healthcare providers and insurance companies consider cost-effectiveness and substitutability when selecting drugs. Lacking significant technological lock-in or integration requirements, the resistance for patients, doctors, or payers to switch to alternative treatment options is not substantial, making it difficult for the company to rely on switching costs to retain customers."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals 的業務模式幾乎不存在網絡效應。其藥物銷售主要基於個別患者的醫療需求，而非用戶間的互動或連接。公司無法從用戶數量的增加中獲得邊際效益遞增的優勢。與科技平台或社交媒體不同，其產品的價值不隨用戶數量的增長而提升，因此網絡效應無法構成其護城河。","comment_en":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals' business model exhibits virtually no network effects. Its drug sales are primarily based on individual patient medical needs, rather than user interactions or connections. The company cannot gain advantages from increasing marginal returns with a growing user base. Unlike tech platforms or social media, the value of its products does not increase with the number of users, thus network effects cannot form its moat."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals 在規模成本優勢方面表現平平。雖然其核心產品 Setmelanotide 針對罕見病，市場規模相對有限，但其生產成本可能因專業性而較高。隨著銷售量的增加，理論上單位生產成本會下降，但由於其利基市場的特性，規模效應的邊際效益遞減明顯。與大型製藥公司相比，其在採購、生產和分銷方面的成本控制能力較弱，難以形成顯著的成本壁壘。","comment_en":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals' performance in terms of cost advantage through scale is mediocre. Although its core product, Setmelanotide, targets rare diseases with a relatively limited market size, its production costs might be higher due to specialization. As sales volume increases, unit production costs theoretically decrease, but due to the niche nature of its market, the marginal benefit of economies of scale diminishes significantly. Compared to large pharmaceutical companies, its cost control capabilities in procurement, production, and distribution are weaker, making it difficult to form a significant cost barrier."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals 並不具備獨特的地理資產或寡占市場地位。其業務主要集中在生物製藥領域，產品的銷售和分銷遍及全球主要市場，並無特定地理區域的顯著優勢。同時，雖然其產品針對罕見病，但並非處於寡占的市場結構，仍面臨潛在的競爭者和替代療法。因此，獨特的地理資產或利基寡占無法構成其護城河。","comment_en":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals does not possess unique geographical assets or a niche oligopolistic market position. Its business is primarily focused on the biopharmaceutical sector, with product sales and distribution across major global markets, lacking significant advantages in any specific geographical region. Furthermore, although its product targets rare diseases, it does not operate in an oligopolistic market structure and still faces potential competitors and alternative therapies. Therefore, unique geographical assets or niche oligopoly do not constitute its moat."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals 的營運效率尚可，但未達頂尖水準。公司在藥物研發、臨床試驗和商業化方面展現了一定的執行力，特別是在罕見病領域取得藥品批准。然而，其持續的虧損和負的 ROE、ROA 表明其營運效率仍有提升空間，未能有效轉化為持續的盈利能力。與行業內效率極高的公司相比，其在成本控制和資源利用方面仍有差距，營運效率對其護城河的貢獻有限。","comment_en":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals' operational efficiency is acceptable but not top-tier. The company demonstrates a certain level of execution in drug R&D, clinical trials, and commercialization, particularly in obtaining drug approvals for rare diseases. However, its persistent losses and negative ROE/ROA indicate room for improvement in operational efficiency, failing to effectively translate into sustained profitability. Compared to highly efficient companies in the industry, it still has gaps in cost control and resource utilization, limiting the contribution of operational efficiency to its moat."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":4,"comment_zh":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals 的資本配置能力有待觀察。公司擁有相對充裕的現金儲備，這為其未來的研發和市場拓展提供了支持。然而，其歷史上的巨額虧損和負的股東權益報酬率，顯示過去的資本配置決策並未帶來理想的回報。管理層需要在確保現金流的同時，更有效地將資源投入到能夠產生可持續利潤的項目上。目前來看，其資本配置策略尚未形成顯著的護城河。","comment_en":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals' capital allocation capability remains to be observed. The company possesses relatively ample cash reserves, which provide support for its future R&D and market expansion. However, its historical substantial losses and negative return on equity indicate that past capital allocation decisions have not yielded ideal returns. Management needs to more effectively invest resources into projects that generate sustainable profits while ensuring cash flow. Currently, its capital allocation strategy has not yet formed a significant moat."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals 的客戶留存率相對較低。雖然 Setmelanotide 的療效對特定患者群體至關重要，但其高昂的價格和潛在的副作用可能影響長期使用意願。此外，罕見病領域的患者群體相對固定，且隨著時間推移，可能出現新的治療選擇。公司缺乏能夠鎖定客戶的長期合約或服務，客戶忠誠度主要依賴於藥物的療效和可及性，這使得客戶留存壁壘不強。","comment_en":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals' customer retention rate is relatively low. While the efficacy of Setmelanotide is crucial for specific patient groups, its high price and potential side effects might affect long-term usage willingness. Furthermore, the patient population in the rare disease field is relatively fixed, and over time, new treatment options may emerge. The company lacks long-term contracts or services that can lock in customers; customer loyalty primarily depends on the drug's efficacy and accessibility, making the customer retention barrier weak."},"m10_durability":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals 的業務可持續性面臨挑戰。其高度依賴單一核心產品 Setmelanotide，這使得公司面臨較大的產品集中風險。雖然該產品在特定罕見病治療領域具有先發優勢，但其長期市場地位受到專利到期、潛在競爭以及藥品生命週期等因素的影響。公司需要持續投入研發，拓展產品線，以應對未來的不確定性，目前其業務模式的可持續性尚不夠穩固。","comment_en":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals' business sustainability faces challenges. Its high dependence on the single core product, Setmelanotide, exposes the company to significant product concentration risk. Although this product has a first-mover advantage in treating specific rare diseases, its long-term market position is affected by factors such as patent expiration, potential competition, and the drug's lifecycle. The company needs to continuously invest in R&D and expand its product pipeline to address future uncertainties. Currently, the sustainability of its business model is not sufficiently robust."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals 的經濟護城河相當薄弱，主要依賴於其核心藥物 Setmelanotide 的專利保護（M2），這提供了短期的市場獨佔性。然而，其品牌定價權（M1）、轉換成本（M3）、網絡效應（M4）、規模成本（M5）、地理資產（M6）、客戶留存（M9）及業務可持續性（M10）均表現不佳。儘管營運效率（M7）和資本配置（M8）尚可，但不足以彌補其他方面的劣勢。整體而言，該公司缺乏巴菲特所尋求的持久競爭優勢，其商業模式更接近於商品型，易受市場變化和競爭影響。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals' economic moat is considerably weak, primarily relying on the patent protection for its core drug, Setmelanotide (M2), which provides short-term market exclusivity. However, its brand pricing power (M1), switching costs (M3), network effects (M4), cost advantages from scale (M5), geographical assets (M6), customer retention (M9), and business sustainability (M10) all perform poorly. Although operational efficiency (M7) and capital allocation (M8) are acceptable, they are insufficient to compensate for weaknesses in other areas. Overall, the company lacks the durable competitive advantages sought by Buffett, and its business model is closer to commodity-like, easily affected by market changes and competition.","evidenceHash":"e7ae86021c7492656ea3ba3731d57b1808717c09c4dbcfe119c61d1bfa25f492","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Vertex AI"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null,"evidenceHash":"e7ae86021c7492656ea3ba3731d57b1808717c09c4dbcfe119c61d1bfa25f492","currentEvidenceHash":"e7ae86021c7492656ea3ba3731d57b1808717c09c4dbcfe119c61d1bfa25f492"},"fScore":{"score":5,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"superRobust","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-08T13:00:26.108Z","evidenceHash":"7e94eae1b815f60b9827064a692967a997e9ad8d7449d45d577e1b6a869558d0"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"highRisk","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-08T13:00:26.108Z","evidenceHash":"7e94eae1b815f60b9827064a692967a997e9ad8d7449d45d577e1b6a869558d0"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/RYTM.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/RYTM.png","website":"https://www.rhythmtx.com","ceo":"David Meeker","full_time_employees":"414","description":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals, Inc. is a biopharmaceutical company with commercial products, dedicated to the discovery, development, and market launch of therapies addressing rare genetic conditions that cause obesity. Its leading pharmaceutical, IMCIVREE, functions as a powerful agonist of the melanocortin-4 receptor (MC4R). This medication is indicated for treating obesity stemming from deficiencies in pro-opiomelanocortin (POMC), proprotein convertase subtilisin/kexin type 1 (PCSK1), or the leptin receptor (LEPR), alongside its use in patients with Bardet-Biedl and Alström syndromes. Furthermore, the company is progressing setmelanotide (the active compound in IMCIVREE) through Phase II clinical trials. These studies are evaluating its potential for a broader spectrum of applications, including obesity caused by heterozygous POMC or LEPR deficiencies, steroid receptor coactivator 1 (SRC1) deficiency, SH2B1 deficiency, MC4 receptor deficiency, and obesity associated with Smith-Magenis syndrome, POMC epigenetic disorders, and other MC4R-related conditions. Rhythm Pharmaceuticals holds a collaborative research agreement with the Clinical Registry Investigating Bardet-Biedl Syndrome. The firm, headquartered in Boston, Massachusetts, was established in 2008 and changed its name from Rhythm Metabolic, Inc. to Rhythm Pharmaceuticals, Inc. in October 2015.","description_en":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals, Inc. is a biopharmaceutical company with commercial products, dedicated to the discovery, development, and market launch of therapies addressing rare genetic conditions that cause obesity. Its leading pharmaceutical, IMCIVREE, functions as a powerful agonist of the melanocortin-4 receptor (MC4R). This medication is indicated for treating obesity stemming from deficiencies in pro-opiomelanocortin (POMC), proprotein convertase subtilisin/kexin type 1 (PCSK1), or the leptin receptor (LEPR), alongside its use in patients with Bardet-Biedl and Alström syndromes. Furthermore, the company is progressing setmelanotide (the active compound in IMCIVREE) through Phase II clinical trials. These studies are evaluating its potential for a broader spectrum of applications, including obesity caused by heterozygous POMC or LEPR deficiencies, steroid receptor coactivator 1 (SRC1) deficiency, SH2B1 deficiency, MC4 receptor deficiency, and obesity associated with Smith-Magenis syndrome, POMC epigenetic disorders, and other MC4R-related conditions. Rhythm Pharmaceuticals holds a collaborative research agreement with the Clinical Registry Investigating Bardet-Biedl Syndrome. The firm, headquartered in Boston, Massachusetts, was established in 2008 and changed its name from Rhythm Metabolic, Inc. to Rhythm Pharmaceuticals, Inc. in October 2015.","description_zh":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals, Inc.（美股代碼：RYTM）為 Healthcare 領域之重要企業，專注於 Biotechnology 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"222 Berkeley Street","city":"Boston","state":"MA","zip":"02116","country":"US","phone":"857 264 4280","full_address":"222 Berkeley Street, Boston, MA 02116, US","range_52w":"74.5-122.2","year_high":122.2,"year_low":74.5,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":74.5,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-09-14","name":"Meeker David P","title":"director, officer: President and CEO","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":50000,"price":6.05,"total_val":0.3},{"date":"2026-09-14","name":"Meeker David P","title":"director, officer: President and CEO","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":6439,"price":101.75,"total_val":0.66},{"date":"2026-09-14","name":"Meeker David P","title":"director, officer: President and CEO","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":30746,"price":102.35,"total_val":3.15},{"date":"2026-09-14","name":"Meeker David P","title":"director, officer: President and CEO","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":8698,"price":103.43,"total_val":0.9},{"date":"2026-09-14","name":"Meeker David P","title":"director, officer: President and CEO","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":1817,"price":104.55,"total_val":0.19},{"date":"2026-09-14","name":"Meeker David P","title":"director, officer: President and CEO","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":2300,"price":105.19,"total_val":0.24},{"date":"2026-09-14","name":"Meeker David P","title":"director, officer: President and CEO","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":50000,"price":6.05,"total_val":0.3},{"date":"2026-09-01","name":"Smith Hunter C","title":"officer: Chief Financial Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":57187,"price":25.79,"total_val":1.47},{"date":"2026-09-01","name":"Smith Hunter C","title":"officer: Chief Financial Officer","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":23072,"price":104.59,"total_val":2.41},{"date":"2026-09-01